---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
---

<Base title="About" description="How Goods Desk researches and compares products.">
  <div class="wrap" style="padding-top:3rem">
    <h1>About Goods Desk</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      We compare everyday products and explain which one fits which situation — and, just as
      often, when you don't need to buy anything at all.
    </p>

    <h2>How we work</h2>
    <p>
      Goods Desk is a small editorial project. For every comparison we start from a specific
      household problem, then narrow the field using the things you can actually verify before
      buying: published specifications, materials and dimensions, warranty terms, price history,
      and the pattern of complaints that shows up across large numbers of verified customer
      reviews.
    </p>
    <p>
      We are explicit about the limits of that method. Unless a page says otherwise, our
      recommendations are based on research and comparison rather than long-term hands-on
      testing. When we haven't used something ourselves, we say so instead of inventing an
      experience. If we can't find enough reliable information to separate two products, we say
      that too.
    </p>

    <h2>How we choose what to cover</h2>
    <p>
      We write about categories where the choice is genuinely confusing: dozens of near-identical
      listings, unclear sizing, or specifications that don't map to how the thing gets used at
      home. Categories where one obvious option wins are not worth an article, so we skip them.
    </p>

    <h2>How we pay for it</h2>
    <p>
      {SITE.disclosureShort} {SITE.amazonDisclosure} Commissions never change which product we
      recommend, and we don't accept payment from manufacturers in exchange for coverage or
      placement. Full details are on our
      <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a> page.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Prices, specifications and availability change constantly. If something on this site is
      wrong or out of date, tell us at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>
      and we'll correct it.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
